<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Willem Adriaan van der Stel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1664">1664</a>–1733</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Willem Adriaan van der Stel succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-van-der-stel">Simon van der Stel</a> as governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, serving from 1699 to 1707. He and other officials used their positions to build up large private farms, notably his estate of Vergelegen, and to dominate the colony's markets. Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burgher</a> settlers protested to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>, which dismissed him in 1707.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/willem-adriaan-van-der-stel.jpg" alt="Willem Adriaan van der Stel" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Weenix · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Simon_van_der_Stel_and_his_son_Willem_Adriaan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
